{%- comment -%}
  Rendered once in layout/theme.liquid, just before </head>:
    {% render 'purelane-head' %}

  Fonts are self-hosted on the Shopify CDN instead of Google Fonts: no extra
  DNS/TLS round trips to two third-party hosts, and the files are preloaded.
  Outfit and Inter (SIL OFL 1.1) as variable fonts, latin subset, one file each
  for every weight. The rupee sign isn't in the latin subset, so each family
  gets a ~1 KB file containing only U+20B9, instead of the 15-85 KB
  latin-ext files that would otherwise load just for "₹".
  preload_tag also sends the preload as a Link header, so Shopify can hint
  the fonts before the HTML is parsed.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'purelane-outfit-latin.woff2' | asset_url | preload_tag: as: 'font', type: 'font/woff2', crossorigin: 'anonymous' }}
{{ 'purelane-inter-latin.woff2' | asset_url | preload_tag: as: 'font', type: 'font/woff2', crossorigin: 'anonymous' }}
<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Outfit'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 100 900; font-display: swap;
    src: url('{{ 'purelane-outfit-latin.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA, U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193, U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Outfit'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 100 900; font-display: swap;
    src: url('{{ 'purelane-outfit-rupee.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+20B9;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Inter'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 100 900; font-display: swap;
    src: url('{{ 'purelane-inter-latin.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA, U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193, U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Inter'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 100 900; font-display: swap;
    src: url('{{ 'purelane-inter-rupee.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+20B9;
  }
</style>
{%- if template.name == 'index' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Home page only: the header floats over the hero as in the prototype.
    Sticky with a negative bottom margin equal to its own height, so the hero
    slides underneath and the pill stays pinned while scrolling. Pure CSS, no
    scroll listener. Set Header > Sticky header to "None" so Dawn's own sticky
    script doesn't also position it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    One continuous backdrop behind the whole home page, fixed to the viewport
    like the prototype's scene layer, instead of each section painting its own
    gradient (which left hard seams where one section's dark bottom met the
    next section's light top). It doesn't depend on section order, so
    reordering or removing sections can't break it. A section can still set
    its own background in the editor.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <style>
    .section-header { position: sticky; top: 10px; z-index: 40; margin-bottom: -62px; }
    .section-header .header-wrapper { background: transparent; }
    html { background: #eaf8ee; }
    body.gradient, body { background: transparent; }
    body::before {
      content: ""; position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: -1; pointer-events: none;
      background: linear-gradient(178deg, #fbfffb 0%, #e3f6e8 30%, #c9ebd3 65%, #aedfbf 100%);
    }
    .hero-banner { --hero-bg: transparent; }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}
{{ 'purelane-base.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'purelane-reveal.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
